{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/hero — the first screen.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     .ns-hero--split makes .ns-band__inner a two-column grid. Below 64rem it
     collapses to one column with the WORDS FIRST — NSDS's rule, and the
     reason the mark is second in the source rather than positioned there.

     ── THE COPY IS GHOST'S, NOT A THEME SETTING ─────────────────────────────
     The headline is {{@site.title}} and the lede is {{@site.description}},
     both edited in Admin → Settings → General. There is no hero_title custom
     setting: it would be a SECOND place to write the site's name, the two
     would drift, and only one of them feeds meta tags, RSS and search.

     ── NO LOGO ABOVE THE HEADLINE, AND THAT IS THE POINT ────────────────────
     The publication logo was here and has been taken out. THE ANIMATED MARK
     IS THE LOGO — same cloud, same hands — so a static copy stacked above the
     headline put the identical mark on screen twice, three times counting the
     one in the bar. On a phone, where the split collapses and the two sit in
     one column, it read as a stutter: mark, name, then the same mark again.

     One mark per screen. The bar carries the small lockup, the hero carries
     the animated one, and the headline is the name in type — which is also
     the only version of it that is selectable, translatable and legible at
     360px.

     ── THE FORM, NOT A BUTTON ───────────────────────────────────────────────
     On a site with almost no archive the email address IS the conversion, and
     a button to Portal costs a click and a modal before anyone can act. It is
     capped at 26rem: a full-width field next to a 40px button reads as a
     search bar, and the pair has to look like a subscription.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-hero ns-hero--split ns-hero--tall ns-band--dark ns-band--grid sp-hero--wide">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">

        <div>
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Learn Salesforce, properly"}}</span>

            <h1 class="ns-hero__title">{{@site.title}}</h1>

            {{#if @site.description}}
                <p class="ns-hero__lede">{{@site.description}}</p>
            {{/if}}

            {{#if @site.members_enabled}}
                {{> "home/subscribe-form"}}
            {{else}}
                <div class="ns-hero__actions">
                    <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--white" href="#latest">
                        {{> "icons/arrow-right"}} {{t "See what's here so far"}}
                    </a>
                </div>
            {{/if}}

            <span class="ns-hero__proof">{{t "Free · no spam · unsubscribe any time"}}</span>
        </div>

        {{!-- Second in the source so it lands UNDER the words when the grid
             collapses.

             It CENTRES on a phone and sits right on the split. Right-aligned
             in a single column it hangs off the text's edge with nothing to
             align to, which reads as a layout that broke rather than one that
             stacked. lg: is 64rem, the width NSDS collapses the split at.

             ── THE ANIMATED STING IS GONE, AND WHAT REPLACED IT ─────────────
             This slot held components/logo-sting: the 4-second broadcast mark
             with 307 animated India dots, eleven keyframe tracks and a 9s
             loop. It is a beautiful thing and it was doing the wrong job
             here. A hero mark is looked at once, for about as long as it
             takes to read the headline beside it, and a nine-second loop is
             built to be WATCHED — so it was either still mid-entrance when
             the reader had already moved on, or it was pulling attention back
             off the headline every nine seconds, forever.

             components/logo-mark is the same geometry, reversed, still. One
             glance is enough, it is legible the moment it paints rather than
             two seconds in, and it costs no animation frames on a page that
             already has a drifting grid behind it.

             The sting is NOT deleted — partials/components/logo-sting.hbs and
             its CSS both stay. It belongs on a splash, an about page, or an
             intro card, where being watched is the point. --}}
        <div class="ns-hero__media max-w-52 mx-auto mt-8 lg:max-w-80 lg:mx-0 lg:ms-auto lg:mt-0">
            {{> "components/logo-mark"}}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
